\q1 Let them gather themselves, all of them; let them stand.
\q2 They will fear; they will have shame together.
\b
\q1 \v 12 The craftsman of iron {has} a tool,
\q2 and he works over the coal,
\q1 and he forms it with hammers,
\q2 and he works it with the arm of his strength.
\q1 He also hungers, and there is no strength;
\q2 he does not drink water, and he tires.
\q1 \v 13 The craftsman of wood stretches out a line;
\q2 he marks it with ochre.
\q1 He makes it with chisels,
\q2 and he marks it with a compass.
\q1 And he makes it like the form of a man,
\q2 like the beauty of mankind, to dwell {in} a house.
\q1 \v 14 He cuts down cedars for it,
