\q2 he prostrates {himself} to it and bows down,
\q1 and he prays to it and says,
\q2 “Deliver me, for you {are} my god.”
\q1 \v 18 They do not know, and they do not understand,
\q2 for one has plastered their eyes from seeing,
\q2 their hearts from considering.
\q1 \v 19 And none sets to his heart,
\q2 and {there is} no knowledge and no understanding to say,
\q1 “Half of it, I burned in the fire,
\q2 and I also baked bread on its coals;
\q2 I roasted flesh and ate.
\q1 And shall I make its remainder into an abomination?
\q2 Shall I prostrate {myself} to the product of a tree?”
\q1 \v 20 He grazes {on} ashes; a deceived heart turns him aside,
\q2 so he does not deliver his soul,
\q1 and he does not say,
\q2 “{Is} not falsehood in my right hand?”
\b
\q1 \v 21 “Remember these {things}, Jacob,
\q2 and Israel, for you {are} my servant.
\q1 I formed you; you {are} a servant to me.
\q2 Israel, you will not be forgotten by me.
\q1 \v 22 I have wiped away your transgressions like a cloud,
\q2 and like a cloud your sins.
\q1 Return to me,
\q2 for I have redeemed you.”
\b
\q1 \v 23 Sing, heavens, for Yahweh has done {this};
\q2 shout, depths of the earth!
