\q1 Behold, I, I was left by myself;
\q2 these, where {are} they {from}?’”
\p
\v 22 Thus says the Lord Yahweh:
\q1 “Behold, I will lift up my hand to the nations,
\q2 and I will raise my banner to the peoples.
\q1 And they will bring your sons in {their} laps,
\q2 and your daughters will be carried on {their} shoulders.
\q1 \v 23 And kings will be the ones fostering you,
\q2 and their princesses, the ones nursing you.
\q1 Nostrils {to} the earth, they will prostrate themselves to you,
\q2 and they will lick the dust of your feet.
\q1 And you will know that I {am} Yahweh;
\q2 who will not have shame, the ones waiting for me.”
\b
\q1 \v 24 Will the spoil be taken from a warrior,
\q2 or if the captive of the righteous will be rescued?
\m
\v 25 For thus says Yahweh,
\q1 “Even the captive of a warrior will be taken,
\q2 and the spoil of the terrible will be rescued.
\q1 And I, I will contend with your contender,
\q2 and I, I will save your sons.
\q1 \v 26 And I will make your oppressors eat their flesh,
\q2 and they will become drunk {with} their blood as {with} new wine.
\q1 And all flesh will know
\q2 that I, Yahweh, {am} your Savior
\q2 and your Redeemer, the Mighty One of Jacob.”
\c 50
\p
\v 1 Thus says Yahweh,
\q1 “Where is this, the writing of divorce of your mother,
\q2 whom I sent her away?
\q1 Or who {is it} among my creditors
\q2 to whom I sold you?
\q1 Behold, you were sold because of your iniquities,
\q2 and your mother was sent away because of your transgressions.
\q1 \v 2 Why did I come, and there was no man?
\q2 I called, but there was none answering.
\q1 Being short, is my hand too short for redemption?
\q2 Or if there is no power in me to deliver?
\q1 Behold, with my rebuke I dry up the sea.
\q2 I make rivers a wilderness;
\q1 their fish stink from there being no water,
\q2 and they die of thirst.
\q1 \v 3 I clothe the heavens {with} darkness,
\q2 and I make sackcloth their covering.”
\b
\q1 \v 4 The Lord Yahweh has given to me a tongue of the learned,
\q2 to know to sustain the weary {with} a word.
\q1 He awakens {me} in the morning;
\q2 in the morning he awakens for me
\q2 an ear to hear like the learned.
\q1 \v 5 The Lord Yahweh has opened for me an ear,
\q2 and I, I did not rebel;
\q2 I did not turn backward.
\q1 \v 6 I gave my back to the ones striking,
\q2 and my cheeks to the ones plucking;
\q1 I did not hide my face
\q2 from disgraces and spitting.
\q1 \v 7 But the Lord Yahweh helps me;
\q2 therefore I am not disgraced.
\q1 Therefore I set my face like flint,
\q2 and I know that I will not have shame.
\q1 \v 8 The one justifying me is near.
\q2 Who will contend with me? Let us stand together!
\q1 Who {is} the master of my judgment?
\q2 Let him come near to me!
\q1 \v 9 Behold, the Lord Yahweh will help me.
\q2 Who {is} he {who} condemns me?
\q1 Behold, all of them will wear out like a garment;
\q2 the moth will devour them.
\b
\q1 \v 10 Who among you fears Yahweh,
\q2 hearing the voice of his servant,
\q1 who walks in darknesses
\q2 and there is no brightness for him?
\q1 Let him trust in the name of Yahweh,
\q2 and let him support himself on his God.
\q1 \v 11 Behold, all of you kindlers of fire,
\q2 ones girding on torches,
\q1 walk in the light of your fire
\q2 and in the torches you have kindled!
\q1 This will be for you from my hand:
\q2 you will lie down in anguish.
\c 51
\q1 \v 1 “Listen to me, pursuers of righteousness,
\q2 seekers of Yahweh.
\q1 Look to the rock {from which} you were hewn
\q2 and to the hole of the pit {from which} you were dug.
\q1 \v 2 Look to Abraham your father
\q2 and to Sarah, she bore you;
\q1 for I called him, one,
\q2 and I blessed him and made him many.”
\q1 \v 3 For Yahweh will comfort Zion;
\q2 he will comfort all of her desolations,
\q1 and he will make her wilderness like Eden
\q2 and her desert plain like the garden of Yahweh.
\q1 Joy and gladness will be found in her,
\q2 thanksgiving and the voice of song.
\q1 \v 4 “Attend to me, my people,
\q2 and listen to me, my nation,
\q1 for law will go out from me,
\q2 and I will make my justice rest for a light of the peoples.
\q1 \v 5 My righteousness {is} near;
\q2 my salvation will go out,
\q2 and my arms will judge the peoples.
\q1 The coastlands will wait for me,
\q2 and they will wait for my arm.
\q1 \v 6 Lift up your eyes to the heavens
\q2 and look to the earth beneath,
\q1 for the heavens will be dissipated like smoke,
\q2 and the earth will wear out like a garment,
\q2 and its dwellers will die like thus.
\q1 But my salvation will be forever,
\q2 and my righteousness will not be dismayed.
\q1 \v 7 Listen to me, knowers of righteousness,
\q2 people {with} my law in their heart.
\q1 May you not fear the reproach of man,
\q2 and may you not be dismayed by their revilings.
\q1 \v 8 For the moth will devour them like a garment,
\q2 and the grub will devour them like wool;
\q1 but my righteousness will be forever,
\q2 and my salvation, to the generation of generations.”
\b
\q1 \v 9 Awake, awake, put on strength,
\q2 arm of Yahweh!
\q1 Awake as in the days of antiquity,
\q2 the generations of eternities.
\q1 {Was} it not you, the one having hewn Rahab in pieces,
\q2 the one having pierced the sea monster?
\q1 \v 10 {Was} it not you, the one having dried up the sea,
\q2 the waters of the great deep,
\q1 he {who} made the depths of the sea
\q2 a way for the redeemed to pass through?
\q1 \v 11 And the ransomed of Yahweh will return
\q2 and come {to} Zion with singing,
\q2 and joy of eternity {will be} on their heads.
\q1 Gladness and joy will overtake {them};
\q2 sorrow and sighing will flee.
\q1 \v 12 “I, I {am} he, the one comforting you.
\q1 Who {are} you, that you should be afraid of man—he will die—
\q2 and of the son of man—he is given up {like} grass—
\q1 \v 13 that you should forget Yahweh your maker,
\q2 the one having stretched out the heavens and having founded the earth;
\q1 that you should fear continually, all of the day,
\q2 from the face of the heat of the oppressor
\q2 as he prepares to destroy?
\q1 But where {is} the heat of the oppressor?
\q1 \v 14 The stooping one hastens to be opened,
\q2 and he will not die in the pit,
\q2 and he will not lack his bread.
\q1 \v 15 And I {am} Yahweh your God,
\q2 the one making the sea rest when its waves roar—
\q2 Yahweh of Armies {is} his name.
\q1 \v 16 And I have put my words in your mouth,
\q2 and I have covered you with the shadow of my hand,
\q1 to plant the heavens and to found the earth
\q2 and to say to Zion, ‘You {are} my people.’”
\q1 \v 17 Awaken yourself! Awaken yourself!
\q2 Arise, Jerusalem,
\q1 {you} who drank from the hand of Yahweh the cup of his heat;
\q2 you drank the goblet of the cup of staggering, you drained {it}.
\q1 \v 18 There is no one guiding her
\q2 from all of the sons she bore,
\q1 and there is no one holding her hand
\q2 from all of the sons she raised.
\q1 \v 19 These two are meeting you—
\q2 who will sympathize with you?—
\q1 destruction and breaking,
\q2 and famine and the sword;
\q2 who will comfort you?
\q1 \v 20 Your sons are enwrapped;
\q2 they lie at the head of all of the streets
\q2 like an antelope {in} a net,
\q1 being full {of} the heat of Yahweh,
\q2 the rebuke of your God.
\q1 \v 21 Therefore hear this, please,
\q2 poor and drunken, but not from wine.
\q1 \v 22 Thus says your Lord Yahweh,
\q2 and your God, he contends {for} his people:
\q1 “Behold, I have taken from your hand
\q2 the cup of staggering,
\q1 the goblet of the cup of my heat;
\q2 you will not add to drink it again.
\q1 \v 23 And I will put it in the hand of the ones grieving you,
\q2 who said to your soul, ‘Lie prostrate, that we may pass over.’
\q1 And you made your back like the earth,
\q2 and like the street, for the ones passing over.”
\c 52
\q1 \v 1 Awake, awake,
\q2 put on your strength, Zion!
\q1 Put on the garments of your beauty,
\q2 Jerusalem, city of holiness,
\q1 for the uncircumcised or the unclean
\q2 will not add, he will {not} enter you again.
\q1 \v 2 Shake yourself from the dust;
\q2 arise, sit, Jerusalem.
\q1 Loosen yourself {from} the bonds of your neck,
\q2 captive daughter of Zion.
\p
\v 3 For thus says Yahweh,
\q1 “You were sold for nothing,
\q2 and not with silver will you be redeemed.”
\p
\v 4 For thus says the Lord Yahweh,
\q1 “My people went down to Egypt at the first to sojourn there,
\q2 and Assyria oppressed him for nothing.
\q1 \v 5 And now, what to me here?”—the declaration of Yahweh—
\q1 “For my people is taken for nothing.
\q2 Its rulers howl”—the declaration of Yahweh—
\q1 “and continually, all of the day,
\q2 my name is being despised.
\q1 \v 6 Therefore, my people will know my name;
\q2 therefore, on that day, that I {am} he, the one speaking,
\q2 behold me.”
\b
\q1 \v 7 How they are beautiful on the mountains,
\q2 the feet of the one heralding,
\q1 the one making {one} hear peace,
\q2 the one heralding good,
\q2 the one making {one} hear salvation,
\q2 the one saying to Zion, “Your God reigns”!
\q1 \v 8 The voice of your watchmen!
\q2 They lift up a voice;
\q2 they sing joyfully together,
\q1 for eye to eye they will look upon
\q2 the returning of Yahweh {to} Zion.
\q1 \v 9 Break forth, sing joyfully together,
\q2 desolations of Jerusalem,
\q1 for Yahweh has comforted his people,
\q2 he has redeemed Jerusalem.
\q1 \v 10 Yahweh has bared the arm of his holiness
\q2 to the eyes of all of the nations,
\q1 and all of the ends of the earth will see
\q2 the salvation of our God.
\b
\q1 \v 11 Turn aside, turn aside, go out from there!
\q2 May you not touch the unclean!
\q1 Go out from its midst;
\q2 purify yourselves, bearers of the vessels of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 12 For you will not go out in haste,
\q2 and you will not go in flight,
\q1 for Yahweh will be going to your faces,
\q2 and the God of Israel will be assembling you.
\b
\q1 \v 13 “Behold, my servant will succeed;
\q2 he will be high, and he will be lifted up,
\q2 and he will be very lofty.
\q1 \v 14 Just as many will marvel at you—
\q2 so from a man {will be} the disfigurement of his appearance,
\q2 and his form, from the sons of man—
\q1 \v 15 so he will sprinkle many nations.
\q2 Kings will shut their mouths because of him,
\q1 for what had not been told to them, they will see,
\q2 and what they had not heard, they will understand.”
\c 53
\q1 \v 1 Who will believe our report,
\q2 and to whom will the arm of Yahweh be revealed?
\q1 \v 2 And he grew up like a shoot to his face
\q2 and like a root from ground of dryness.
\q1 No form {was} to him, and no splendor,
\q2 that we might see him,
\q1 and no appearance,
\q2 that we should desire him.
\q1 \v 3 He was despised and rejected of men,
\q2 a man of sorrows and acquainted of grief,
\q1 and like a hiding of faces from him,
\q2 he was despised, and we did not esteem him.
\q1 \v 4 Surely he, he bore our griefs,
\q2 and our sorrows, he carried them.
\q1 But we, we esteemed him stricken,
\q2 struck of God, and afflicted.
\q1 \v 5 But he was pierced for our transgressions,
\q2 crushed for our iniquities.
\q1 The discipline of our peace {was} on him,
\q2 and by his wounds it is healed for us.
\q1 \v 6 All of us have strayed like sheep;
\q2 we have turned, a man to his way,
\q1 and Yahweh has made the iniquity of all of us
\q2 land on him.
\b
\q1 \v 7 He was oppressed, and he was afflicted,
\q2 and he did not open his mouth.
\q1 He was led like a lamb to the slaughter,
\q2 and as a ewe silences itself to the face of its shearers,
\q2 so he did not open his mouth.
\q1 \v 8 By coercion and by judgment he was taken,
\q2 and who will consider his generation?
\q1 For he was cut off from the land of the living.
\q2 From the transgression of my people, affliction {was} to him.
\q1 \v 9 And one made his grave with the wicked,
\q2 but {he was} with a rich {one} in his deaths
\q1 because he had done no violence
\q2 and deceit {was} not in his mouth.
\q1 \v 10 But Yahweh was pleased to crush him; he made {him} grieve.
\q2 When you make his soul a guilt offering,
\q2 he will see seed, he will lengthen days,
\q1 and the pleasure of Yahweh will prosper in his hand.
\q1 \v 11 From the trouble of his soul, he will see, he will have enough.
\q2 “By his knowledge, my righteous servant will justify many,
\q2 and he, he will bear their iniquities.
\q1 \v 12 Therefore I will divide for him among the great,
\q2 and with the mighty he will divide the spoil,
\q1 because he exposed his soul to death,
\q2 and he was numbered with transgressors.
\q1 And he, he bore the sin of many,
\q2 and he intercedes for transgressors.”
\c 54
\q1 \v 1 “Sing joyfully, barren {one}, she has not birthed,
\q2 break forth {into} joyful singing,
\q2 and cry aloud, she has not writhed,
\q1 for the sons of the one being desolate {are} more than
\q2 the sons of the married,” says Yahweh.
\q1 \v 2 “Broaden the place of your tent,
\q2 and may they stretch out the curtains of your dwellings;
\q2 may you not refrain.
\q1 Lengthen your ropes,
\q2 and strengthen your stakes.
\q1 \v 3 For you will break forth to the right and to the left,
\q2 and your seed will dispossess nations,
\q2 and they will make {people} inhabit desolated cities.
\b
\q1 \v 4 May you not fear, for you will not have shame,
\q2 and may you not be humiliated, for you will not display disgrace.
\q1 For you will forget the shame of your youth,
\q2 and you will not remember the disgrace of your widowhood anymore.
\q1 \v 5 For your husband {is} your Maker;
\q2 Yahweh of Armies {is} his name.
\q1 And your Redeemer {is} the Holy One of Israel;
\q2 he is called the God of all of the earth.
\q1 \v 6 For Yahweh has called you like a wife abandoned
\q2 and grieved of spirit,
\q1 and a wife of youth when she has been rejected,”
\q2 says your God.
\q1 \v 7 “For a small moment I abandoned you,
\q2 but with great compassions I will gather you.
\q1 \v 8 In a flood of anger I hid my face
\q2 {for} a moment from you,
\q1 but with covenant faithfulness of eternity I will have compassion on you,”
\q2 says Yahweh your redeemer.
\b
\q1 \v 9 “For this {is} the waters of Noah to me,
\q2 when I swore the waters of Noah would not pass over the earth again;
\q1 thus I have sworn not to be angry with you
\q2 and not to rebuke you.
\q1 \v 10 For the mountains may depart,
\q2 and the hills may shake,
\q1 but my covenant faithfulness will not depart from you,
\q2 and the covenant of my peace will not shake,”
\q2 says Yahweh, the one having compassion on you.
\b
\q1 \v 11 “Poor, tempested, not comforted,
\q2 behold, I am setting your stones in antimony,
\q1 and I will found you with sapphires.
\q1 \v 12 And I will make your battlements rubies
\q2 and your gates into stones of beryl
\q2 and all of your border into stones of delight.
\q1 \v 13 And all of your sons {will be} disciples of Yahweh,
\q2 and great {will be} the peace of your sons.
\q1 \v 14 You will be established in righteousness.
\q2 Be far from oppression, for you will not fear,
\q2 and from terror, for it will not come near to you.
\q1 \v 15 Behold, quarreling, one may quarrel, not from with me;
\q2 whoever quarrels with you will fall before you.
\b
\q1 \v 16 Behold, I, I have created the craftsman
\q2 blowing on a fire of a coal
\q1 and bringing out a weapon for its work,
\q2 and I, I have created the destroyer to destroy.
\q1 \v 17 Every weapon formed against you will not prosper,
\q2 and every tongue rising against you in judgment, you will condemn.
\q1 This {is} the inheritance of the servants of Yahweh
\q2 and their righteousness from me”—the declaration of Yahweh.
\c 55
\q1 \v 1 “Oh, everyone thirsty, go to the waters,
\q2 and to whom {is} no silver, go, buy, and eat!
\q1 And go, buy without silver,
\q2 and without price, wine and milk.
\q1 \v 2 Why do you weigh out silver for {what is} not bread,
\q2 and your labor, for {what is} not to sufficiency?
\q1 Listening, listen to me and eat the good,
\q2 and let your soul be delighted by fatness.
\q1 \v 3 Incline your ear, and go to me.
\q2 Listen, that your soul may live.
\q1 And let me cut with you a covenant of eternity,
\q2 the confirmed covenant faithfulnesses of David.
\q1 \v 4 Behold, I have given him {as} a witness to the peoples,
\q2 a ruler and a commander to the peoples.
\q1 \v 5 Behold, you will call a nation you have not known,
\q2 and a nation, they have not known you, they will run to you,
\q1 because of Yahweh your God,
\q2 and for the Holy One of Israel, for he will glorify you.”
\b
\q1 \v 6 Seek Yahweh while he may be found;
\q2 call on him while he is near.
\q1 \v 7 Let the wicked abandon his way,
\q2 and the man of iniquity, his thoughts,
\q1 and let him return to Yahweh, and he will have compassion on him,
\q2 and to our God, for he will make great to forgive.
\b
\q1 \v 8 “For my thoughts {are} not your thoughts,
\q2 and your ways {are} not my ways”
\q2 —the declaration of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 9 “For {as} the heavens are higher than the earth,
\q2 so my ways are higher than your ways,
\q2 and my thoughts, than your thoughts.
\q1 \v 10 For as the rain and snow come down from the heavens
\q2 and do not return to there
\q1 unless they have saturated the earth
\q2 and made it bring forth and made it sprout,
\q1 and it gives seed to the sower
\q2 and bread to the eater,
\q1 \v 11 so will my word be that goes out from my mouth:
\q2 it will not return to me empty,
\q1 but it will do what I desire,
\q2 and it will accomplish what I send it {to do}.
\q1 \v 12 For you will go out in joy,
\q2 and you will be led in peace.
\q1 The mountains and the hills will break out to your faces {in} singing,
\q2 and all of the trees of the field will clap the palm.
\q1 \v 13 Instead of the thornbush, the cypress will come up,
\q2 and instead of the nettle, the myrtle will come up,
\q1 and it will be to Yahweh for a name,
\q2 for a sign of eternity, it will not be cut off.”
\c 56
\p
\v 1 Thus says Yahweh,
\q1 “Keep justice and do righteousness,
\q2 for my salvation {is} near to coming,
\q2 and my righteousness, to being revealed.
\q1 \v 2 The happiness of the man {who} does this
\q2 and the son of man {who} holds onto it,
\q1 keeping the Sabbath from profaning it
\q2 and keeping his hand from doing any evil!”
\b
\q1 \v 3 And let not the son of the foreigner
\q2 {who} joins himself to Yahweh say,
\q1 saying, “Separating, Yahweh will separate me
\q2 from his people.”
\q1 And let not the eunuch say,
\q2 “Behold, I {am} a dry tree.”
\p
\v 4 For thus says Yahweh,
\q1 “To the eunuchs who keep my Sabbaths
\q2 and choose what I desire
\q2 and are holding onto my covenant,
\q1 \v 5 I will give to them in my house
\q2 and within my walls
\q2 a hand and a name
\q1 better than sons and daughters;
\q2 I will give to him a name of eternity
\q2 that will not be cut off.
\q1 \v 6 And the sons of the foreigner
\q2 joining themselves to Yahweh to serve him
\q1 and to love the name of Yahweh
\q2 to be servants to him,
\q2 everyone keeping the Sabbath from profaning it
\q2 and holding onto my covenant,
\q1 \v 7 I will bring them to the mountain of my holiness,
\q2 and I will make them rejoice in the house of my prayer.
\q1 Their burnt offerings and their sacrifices
\q2 {will be} for acceptance on my altar.
\q1 For my house will be called
\q2 a house of prayer for all of the peoples”
\q1 \v 8 —the declaration of Lord Yahweh,
\q2 the one gathering the outcasts of Israel—
\q1 “yet I will gather to him,
\q2 to his gathered ones.”
\b
\q1 \v 9 Every beast of the field,
\q2 come to devour,
\q2 every beast in the forest!
\q1 \v 10 His watchmen {are} blind, all of them;
\q2 they do not know.
\q1 All of them {are} mute dogs,
\q2 they are not able to bark,
\q1 dreaming, lying down,
\q2 ones loving to sleep.
\q1 \v 11 And the dogs {are} mighty of soul;
\q2 they do not know satiety.
\q1 And they {are} shepherds
\q2 {who} do not know to discern.
\q1 All of them have turned to their way,
\q2 a man to his gain, from his end.
\q1 \v 12 “Come, let me take wine,
\q2 and let us quaff beer,
\q1 and tomorrow will be like this day,
\q2 great, much abundance.”
\c 57
\q1 \v 1 The righteous perishes,
\q2 but there is no man setting {it} on the heart,
\q1 and the men of covenant faithfulness are assembled,
\q2 with no one understanding
\q1 that from the face of evil
\q2 the righteous is assembled.
\q1 \v 2 He enters peace;
\q2 they rest on their beds,
\q2 the one walking {in} his uprightness.
\b
\q1 \v 3 “But you, come near here,
\q2 sons of a sorceress,
\q2 seed of an adulterer, and she whored.
\q1 \v 4 Against whom do you delight yourselves?
\q2 Against whom do you make wide the mouth,
\q2 do you make long the tongue?
\q1 {Are} you not children of transgression,
\q2 seed of falsehood,
\q1 \v 5 ones inflaming yourselves among the oaks,
\q2 under every green tree,
\q1 slaughterers of children in wadis,
\q2 under clefts of rocks?
\q1 \v 6 Among the smooth of the wadi {is} your portion;
\q2 they, they {are} your lot.
\q1 Even to them you pour out a drink offering,
\q2 you raise up a grain offering.
\q2 Shall I relent over these?
\q1 \v 7 You set your bed on a high and uplifted mountain.
\q2 You go up even there to sacrifice a sacrifice.
\q1 \v 8 And you set your memorial
\q2 behind the door and the doorpost.
\q1 For away from me you uncover {yourself} and go up;
\q2 you make wide your bed,
\q1 and you cut {a covenant} for yourself with them.
\q2 You love their bed; you see a hand.
\q1 \v 9 And you turn to Molech with oil,
\q2 and you multiply your perfumes.
\q1 And you send your envoys to faraway,
\q2 and you lower {yourself} to Sheol.
\q1 \v 10 In the greatness of your way you become tired;
\q2 you do not say, ‘Despairing!’
\q1 You find the life of your hand;
\q2 therefore you do not weaken.
\b
\q1 \v 11 And whom do you dread and fear,
\q2 that you lie and do not remember me,
\q2 you do not set to your heart?
\q1 {Is it} not me being silent
\q2 even from eternity
\q2 that you do not fear me?
\q1 \v 12 I, I will declare your righteousness and your deeds,
\q2 and they will not benefit you.
\q1 \v 13 When you cry out, let your collection deliver you!
\q2 But the wind will carry all of them away,
\q2 a breath will take {them}.
\q1 But the one taking refuge in me will inherit the land,
\q2 and he will possess the mountain of my holiness.”
\p
\v 14 And one will say,
\q1 “Build up, build up! Prepare a way!
\q2 Lift the stumbling block from the way of my people!”
\q1 \v 15 For thus says the high and uplifted {one},
\q2 dwelling forever, and holy {is} his name:
\q1 “I dwell {in} the height and {in} the holy,
\q2 and with the crushed and the lowly of spirit,
\q1 to make alive the spirit of the lowly
\q2 and to make alive the heart of the crushed.
\q1 \v 16 For I will not contend to eternity,
\q2 and I will not be angry for ever,
\q1 for the spirit would faint from to my face
\q2 and the breaths I, I have made.
\q1 \v 17 For the iniquity of his gain,
\q2 I was angry, and I struck him;
\q1 I hid, and I was angry,
\q2 but he went backward
\q2 in the way of his heart.
\q1 \v 18 I have seen his ways, and I will heal him,
\q2 and I will lead him,
\q1 and I will restore comforts to him
\q2 and to his mourners,
\q1 \v 19 creating the fruit of the lips.
\q2 Peace, peace to the faraway and to the near,”
\q2 says Yahweh, “and I will heal him.
\q1 \v 20 But the wicked {will be} like the driven sea,
\q2 for it is not able to rest,
\q1 but its waters drive out mud and mire.
\q1 \v 21 There is no peace,” says my God, “for the wicked.”
\c 58
\q1 \v 1 “Call out in the throat; do not refrain.
\q2 Raise your voice like a shofar,
\q1 and declare to my people their transgression,
\q2 and to the house of Jacob, their sins.
\q1 \v 2 Yet day, day they seek me,
\q2 and they delight in the knowledge of my ways,
\q1 like a nation that has done righteousness
\q2 and has not abandoned the judgment of its God.
\q1 They ask me {for} judgments of righteousness;
\q2 they delight in the approach of God.
\q1 \v 3 ‘Why have we fasted, but you have not seen,
\q2 have we humbled our soul, but you have not known?’
\q1 Behold, on the day of your fast, you find pleasure,
\q2 and you oppress all of your laborers.
\q1 \v 4 Behold, you fast for contention and quarrel,
\q2 and to strike with a fist of wickedness.
\q1 You shall not fast as today
\q2 to make {one} hear your voice in the height!
\q1 \v 5 Is the fast, I choose it, like this,
\q2 a day of a man humbling his soul,
\q1 to bow his head like a reed,
\q2 and to spread sackcloth and ashes?
\q1 Do you call this a fast
\q2 and a day of acceptance to Yahweh?
\q1 \v 6 {Is} not this the fast, I choose it:
\q2 to loose the bonds of wickedness,
\q2 to undo the ropes of the yoke,
\q1 and to send the crushed ones free,
\q2 and you shall break every yoke?
\q1 \v 7 {Is it} not to divide your bread to the hungry,
\q2 and you shall bring the wandering poor {into your} house?
\q1 When you see the naked, then you shall cover him,
\q2 and you shall not hide yourself from your flesh.
\q1 \v 8 Then your light will break forth like the dawn,
\q2 and your healing will sprout up quickly.
\q1 And your righteousness will go to your face;
\q2 the glory of Yahweh will assemble you.
\q1 \v 9 Then you will call, and Yahweh will answer;
\q2 you will cry out, and he will say, ‘Behold me.’
\b
\q1 If you remove the yoke from your midst,
\q2 the putting forth of the finger and the speaking of iniquity,
\q1 \v 10 and you bring out your soul to the hungry
\q2 and you satisfy the soul of the poor,
\q1 then your light will rise in the darkness,
\q2 and your gloom {will be} like noon.
\q1 \v 11 And Yahweh will lead you continually,
\q2 and he will satisfy your soul in dry places,
\q1 and he will strengthen your bones,
\q2 and you will be like a watered garden
\q1 and like a spring of water
\q2 whose waters do not deceive.
\q1 \v 12 And {some} from you will build the desolations of eternity;
\q2 you will raise up the foundations of generation and generation,
\q1 and one will call you Repairer of the Breach,
\q2 Restorer of Streets to Dwell In.
\q1 \v 13 If you turn back your foot from the Sabbath,
\q2 {from} doing your pleasures on the day of my holiness,
\q1 and you call the Sabbath a delight,
\q2 the holy of Yahweh, honored,
\q1 and you honor it from doing your ways,
\q2 from finding your pleasure and speaking a word,
\q1 \v 14 then you will delight yourself over Yahweh,
\q2 and I will make you ride on the heights of the earth,
\q1 and I will feed you the inheritance of Jacob your father,”
\q2 for the mouth of Yahweh has spoken.
\c 59
\q1 \v 1 Behold, the hand of Yahweh is not too short to save,
\q2 and his ear, not too heavy to hear.
\q1 \v 2 But your iniquities have been separating
\q2 between you and between your God,
\q1 and your sins have hidden {his} face
\q2 from you from hearing.
\q1 \v 3 For your palms are stained with blood,
\q2 and your fingers, with iniquity.
\q1 Your lips have spoken falsehood;
\q2 your tongue murmurs wickedness.
\q1 \v 4 None is calling in righteousness,
\q2 and none is judging with another in faithfulness,
\q1 trusting in emptiness and speaking falsehood,
\q2 conceiving trouble and birthing iniquity.
\q1 \v 5 They hatch the eggs of a viper,
\q2 and they weave the webs of a spider.
\q1 The one eating of their eggs dies;
\q2 when one is crushed, an adder hatches.
\q1 \v 6 Their webs will not become clothing,
\q2 and they will not cover themselves with their works.
\q1 Their works {are} works of iniquity,
\q2 and a deed of violence {is} in their palms.
\q1 \v 7 Their feet run to evil,
\q2 and they hasten to pour out innocent blood.
\q1 Their thoughts {are} thoughts of iniquity;
\q2 destruction and breaking {are} in their highways.
\q1 \v 8 They do not know the way of peace,
\q2 and there is no justice in their tracks.
\q1 They have made their paths crooked for themselves;
\q2 everyone treading on it does not know peace.
\b
\q1 \v 9 Therefore justice is far from us,
\q2 and righteousness does not overtake us.
\q1 We wait for light, but behold, darkness;
\q2 for brightness, we walk in gloom.
\q1 \v 10 We grope the wall like the blind,
\q2 and like without eyes, we grope.
\q1 We stumble at noon as {in} twilight;
\q2 among the strong, like ones having died.
\q1 \v 11 We growl like bears, all of us,
\q2 and like doves, murmuring, we murmur.
\q1 We wait for justice, but there is none;
\q2 for salvation, it is far from us.
\b
\q1 \v 12 For our transgressions are many before you,
\q2 and our sins, it testifies against us.
\q1 For our transgressions {are} with us,
\q2 and our iniquities, we know them:
\q1 \v 13 rebelling and denying Yahweh,
\q2 and turning away from after our God;
\q1 speaking oppression and revolt,
\q2 conceiving and murmuring words of falsehood from the heart.
\q1 \v 14 And justice is driven back,
\q2 and righteousness stands from faraway.
\q1 For truth stumbles in the open area,
\q2 and uprightness is not able to enter.
\q1 \v 15 And truth is missing,
\q2 and the one turning from evil makes himself plunder.
\b
\q1 And Yahweh saw, and it was evil in his eyes
\q2 that there was no justice.
\q1 \v 16 And he saw that there was no man,
\q2 and he was desolated that there was no intercessor.
\q1 So his arm saved for him,
\q2 and his righteousness, it, it supported him.
\q1 \v 17 And he put on righteousness as a breastplate
\q2 and a helmet of salvation on his head.
\q1 And he put on garments of vengeance {for} clothing,
\q2 and he wrapped {himself} with zeal as a robe.
\q1 \v 18 According to deeds, according to {what} he will repay:
\q2 heat to his adversaries,
\q2 recompense to his enemies;
\q2 he will repay the recompense to the coastlands.
\q1 \v 19 And they will fear the name of Yahweh from the setting,
\q2 and his glory from the rising of the sun;
\q1 for he will come like a narrow stream,
\q2 the wind of Yahweh drives upon it.
\q1 \v 20 “And a redeemer will come to Zion
\q2 and to the ones turning from transgression in Jacob”
\q2 —the declaration of Yahweh.
\p
\v 21 “And {as for} me, this {is} my covenant with them,” says Yahweh. “My Spirit, who {is} upon you, and my words, which I have put in your mouth, will not depart from your mouth or from the mouth of your seed or from the mouth of the seed of your seed,” says Yahweh, “from now and to eternity.”
\c 60
\q1 \v 1 “Arise, shine, for your light has come,
\q2 and the glory of Yahweh has risen upon you.
\q1 \v 2 For behold, darkness will cover the earth,
\q2 and gloom, the peoples;
\q1 but Yahweh will rise upon you,
\q2 and his glory will be seen upon you.
\q1 \v 3 And nations will go to your light,
\q2 and kings, to the brightness of your rising.
\q1 \v 4 Lift up your eyes around and see;
\q2 all of them gather themselves, they come to you.
\q1 Your sons will come from faraway,
\q2 and your daughters will be supported on the side.
\q1 \v 5 Then you will see and be radiant,
\q2 and your heart will fear and broaden,
\q1 for the abundance of the sea will be turned to you;
\q2 the wealth of the nations will come to you.
\q1 \v 6 A multitude of camels will cover you,
\q2 young camels of Midian and Ephah.
\q1 All of them will come from Sheba;
\q2 they will carry gold and frankincense,
\q2 and they will proclaim the praises of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 7 All of the flocks of Kedar will be gathered to you;
\q2 rams of Nebaioth will serve you.
\q1 They will ascend my altar with acceptance,
\q2 and I will glorify the house of my splendor.
\q1 \v 8 Who {are} these? They fly like a cloud,
\q2 and like doves, to their coops.
\q1 \v 9 For the coastlands wait for me,
\q2 and the ships of Tarshish {will be} first,
\q1 to bring your sons from faraway,
\q2 their silver and their gold with them,
\q1 for the name of Yahweh your God,
\q2 and for the Holy One of Israel,
\q2 for he has glorified you.
\q1 \v 10 And sons of foreignness will build your walls,
\q2 and their kings will serve you;
\q1 for in my wrath I struck you,
\q2 but in my favor I will have compassion on you.
\q1 \v 11 And your gates will be open continually;
\q2 day and night they will not be shut,
\q1 to bring to you the wealth of the nations
\q2 and their kings, being led.
\q1 \v 12 For the nation and the kingdom that does not serve you will perish,
\q2 and nations, destroying, they will destroy.
\q1 \v 13 The glory of Lebanon will come to you,
\q2 the cypress, the plane, and the box tree together,
\q1 to beautify the place of my sanctuary,
\q2 and I will glorify the place of my feet.
\q1 \v 14 And they will go to you bowing down,
\q2 the sons of the ones having humbled you,
\q1 and all of the ones having despised you
\q2 will prostrate themselves at the soles of your feet,
\q1 and they will call to you “The City of Yahweh,”
\q2 “Zion of the Holy One of Israel.”
\q1 \v 15 Instead of you being abandoned and hated,
\q2 with no one passing through,
\q1 I will make you a pride of forever,
\q2 a joy of generation and generation.
\q1 \v 16 And you will suck the milk of the nations,
\q2 and you will nurse {at} the breast of kings.
\q1 And you will know that I, Yahweh,
\q2 {am} your Savior and your Redeemer,
\q2 the Mighty One of Jacob.
\q1 \v 17 Instead of bronze, I will bring gold,
\q2 and instead of iron, I will bring silver,
\q1 and instead of wood, bronze,
\q2 and instead of stones, iron.
\q1 And I will appoint peace {as} your governor
\q2 and righteousness {as} your rulers.
\q1 \v 18 Violence will no longer be heard in your land;
\q2 destruction and breaking, within your borders.
\q1 And you will call your walls Salvation,
\q2 and your gates, Praise.
\q1 \v 19 The sun will no longer be to you for light by day,
\q2 and the moon will not give light to you for brightness,
\q1 but Yahweh will be to you for a light of eternity,
\q2 and your God, for your splendor.
\q1 \v 20 Your sun will no longer go in,
\q2 and your moon will not be assembled,
\q1 for Yahweh will be to you for a light of eternity,
\q2 and the days of your mourning will finish.
\q1 \v 21 And your people, all of them {will be} righteous;
\q2 to eternity, they will possess the land,
\q1 the branch of my planting,
\q2 the work of my hands, that I may be glorified.
\q1 \v 22 The small will become a thousand,
\q2 and the little, a strong nation.
\q1 I, Yahweh, will hasten it in its time.”
\c 61
\q1 \v 1 The Spirit of the Lord Yahweh {is} on me
\q2 because Yahweh has anointed me
\q1 to proclaim good news to the poor.
\q2 He has sent me to bind up the broken of heart,
\q1 to call out freedom to the captives,
\q2 and liberation to the bound,
\q1 \v 2 to call out the year of favor of Yahweh,
\q2 and the day of vengeance of our God,
\q2 to comfort all mourners,
\q1 \v 3 to set for the mourners of Zion:
\q2 to give a headdress to them instead of ashes,
\q1 the oil of joy instead of mourning,
\q2 a garment of praise instead of a spirit of dullness.
\q1 And one will call to them “oaks of righteousness,”
\q2 “the planting of Yahweh,”
\q2 that he might be glorified.
\q1 \v 4 And they will build the desolations of eternity;
\q2 they will raise the former devastations.
\q1 And they will renew the cities of desolation,
\q2 the devastations of generation and generation.
\q1 \v 5 And foreigners will stand and will shepherd your flocks,
\q2 and sons of foreignness {will be} your farmers and your vinedressers.
\q1 \v 6 And you, you will be called priests of Yahweh;
\q2 “servants of our God” will be said to you.
\q1 You will eat the wealth of nations,
\q2 and you will boast yourself in their glory.
\q1 \v 7 Instead of your shame, double,
\q2 and {instead of} dishonor, they will shout {over} their portion.
\q1 Therefore in their land they will possess double;
\q2 joy of eternity will be to them.
\b
\q1 \v 8 “For I, Yahweh, am loving justice,
\q2 hating robbery in burnt offering.
\q1 And I will give their recompense in truth,
\q2 and I will cut a covenant of eternity for them.
\q1 \v 9 And their seed will be known among the nations,
\q2 and their offspring, in the midst of the peoples.
\q1 All the ones seeing them will recognize them,
\q2 that they {are} seed Yahweh has blessed.”
\b
\q1 \v 10 Rejoicing, I will rejoice in Yahweh;
\q2 my soul will be glad in my God.
\q1 For he has clothed me {with} garments of salvation;
\q2 he has wrapped me {with} a robe of righteousness,
\q1 as a bridegroom decks {himself} {with} a headdress,
\q2 and as a bride adorns {herself} with her jewels.
\q1 \v 11 For as the earth sends forth its sprout,
\q2 and as a garden makes its sowings sprout,
\q1 so the Lord Yahweh will make righteousness sprout,
\q2 and praise, before all of the nations.
\c 62
\q1 \v 1 For the sake of Zion, I will not be silent,
\q2 and for the sake of Jerusalem, I will not be quiet,
\q1 until its righteousness goes forth like brightness
\q2 and its salvation burns like a torch.
\q1 \v 2 And the nations will see your righteousness,
\q2 and all of the kings, your glory,
\q1 and one will call to you a new name
\q2 that the mouth of Yahweh will designate.
\q1 \v 3 And you will be a crown of beauty in the hand of Yahweh
\q2 and a turban of kingship in the palm of your God.
\q1 \v 4 It will no longer be said of you, “Abandoned,”
\q2 and of your land, it will no longer be said, “Devastation,”
\q1 for it will be called to you, “Hephzibah,”
\q2 and to your land, “Beulah,”
\q1 for Yahweh delights in you,
\q2 and your land will be married.
\q1 \v 5 For a young man marries a young woman;
\q2 your sons will marry you.
\q1 And the rejoicing of a bridegroom over a bride,
\q2 your God will rejoice over you.
\q1 \v 6 I have appointed watchmen on your walls, Jerusalem;
\q1 All of the day and all of the night,
\q2 continually, they will not be silent.
\q1 Ones reminding Yahweh,
\q2 may there not be quiet to you,
\q1 \v 7 and do not give quiet to him,
\q2 until he establishes
\q1 and until he makes Jerusalem
\q2 a praise in the earth.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh has sworn by his right hand
\q2 and by the arm of his strength,
\q1 “If I should give your grain anymore
\q2 {as} food to your enemies,
\q1 and if the sons of foreignness should drink your new wine,
\q2 for which you have labored!
\q1 \v 9 For its collectors will eat it
\q2 and praise Yahweh,
\q1 and its gatherers will drink it
\q2 in the courts of my holiness.”
\q1 \v 10 Pass through, pass through the gates!
\q2 Prepare the way of the people!
\q1 Build up, build up the highway!
\q2 Clear {it} from stone!
\q1 Raise a banner for the peoples!
\q1 \v 11 Behold, Yahweh has made {it} heard to the end of the earth:
\q1 “Say to the daughter of Zion,
\q2 ‘Behold, your salvation is coming!
\q1 Behold, his wage {is} with him,
\q2 and his reward {is} to his face.’”
\q1 \v 12 And they will call to them, “The People of Holiness,”
\q2 “The Redeemed of Yahweh,”
\q1 and to you it will be called, “Sought After,”
\q2 “A City Not Abandoned.”
\c 63
\q1 \v 1 Who {is} this coming from Edom, dyed of garments,
\q2 from Bozrah, this {one}, honored in his clothing,
\q2 bending forward in the greatness of his strength?
\q1 “I, speaking in righteousness,
\q2 mighty to save.”
\q1 \v 2 Why {is} your clothing red
\q2 and your garments, like one treading in a wine press?
\q1 \v 3 “I have trodden a winepress by myself,
\q2 and from the peoples, no man {was} with me.
\q1 And I trod them in my nose,
\q2 and I trampled them in my heat,
\q1 and their juice spattered on my garments,
\q2 and I stained all of my clothes.
\q1 \v 4 For the day of vengeance {was} in my heart,
\q2 and the year of my redeemed ones came.
\q1 \v 5 And I looked, and there was no helper,
\q2 and I was desolated that no one was supporting.
\q1 So my arm saved for me,
\q2 and my heat, it, it supported me.
\q1 \v 6 And I trampled peoples in my nose,
\q2 and I made them drunk in my heat,
\q2 and I brought down their blood to the earth.”
\b
\q1 \v 7 I will make {one} remember the covenant faithfulnesses of Yahweh,
\q2 the praises of Yahweh according to all that Yahweh has rewarded us
\q2 and {his} great goodness to the house of Israel,
\q1 which he has rewarded them according to his compassions
\q2 and according to the greatness of his covenant faithfulness.
\q1 \v 8 And he said, “Surely they {are} my people,
\q2 sons {who} will not deal falsely.”
\q2 And he became a savior for them.
\q1 \v 9 In all of their affliction, he was not afflicted,
\q2 and the angel of his face saved them.
\q1 In his love and in his mercy
\q2 he, he redeemed them,
\q1 and he lifted them up and carried them
\q2 all of the days of eternity.
\q1 \v 10 But they, they rebelled,
\q2 and they grieved the Spirit of his holiness.
\q1 And he turned himself into an enemy of them;
\q2 he, he fought with them.
\q1 \v 11 And his people remembered the days of eternity, {of} Moses,
\q2 “Where {is} the one having brought them up from the sea
\q1 with the shepherds of his flock?
\q2 Where {is} the one having put
\q2 the Spirit of his holiness in his midst,
\q1 \v 12 the one having made the arm of his splendor go
\q2 to the right hand of Moses,
\q1 the one having divided the waters from their faces,
\q2 to make for himself name of eternity,
\q1 \v 13 the one having led them through the depths?
\q2 Like a horse in the wilderness,
\q2 they did not stumble.
\q1 \v 14 Like cattle going down into a valley,
\q2 the Spirit of Yahweh made him rest.
\q1 Thus you led your people,
\q2 to make for yourself a name of splendor.
\q1 \v 15 Look from the heavens and see,
\q2 from the habitation of your holiness and your splendor.
\q1 Where {are} your zeal and your mighty deeds?
\q2 The stirring of your inner parts and your compassions,
\q2 they have restrained themselves from me.
\q1 \v 16 For you {are} our father,
\q2 for Abraham does not know us,
\q2 and Israel does not recognize us.
\q1 You, Yahweh, {are} our father;
\q2 our Redeemer from eternity {is} your name.
\q1 \v 17 Why do you make us wander, Yahweh, from your ways?
\q2 {Why} do you harden our heart from fearing you?
\q1 Return for the sake of your servants,
\q2 the tribes of your inheritance.
\q1 \v 18 For a little, the people of your holiness possessed {it};
\q2 our adversaries have trampled your sanctuary.
\q1 \v 19 We have become from eternity;
\q2 you did not rule over them,
\q2 your name was not called over them.
\c 64
\q1 \v 1 If {only} you would rend the heavens, you would come down!
\q2 From your face the mountains would quake.
\q1 \v 2 As fire kindles brushwood,
\q2 fire boils water,
\q1 to make your name known to your adversaries,
\q2 nations would tremble from your face.
\q1 \v 3 When you did fearful things we did not expect,
\q2 you came down; the mountains quaked from your face.
\q1 \v 4 And from eternity they have not heard,
\q2 they have not listened;
\q1 an eye has not seen a God besides you,
\q2 he works for the one waiting for him.
\q1 \v 5 You meet the one rejoicing and doing righteousness;
\q2 in your ways they remember you.
\q1 Behold, you, you were angry,
\q2 for we had sinned against them {from} eternity,
\q2 so shall we be saved?
\q1 \v 6 And we have become like the unclean, all of us,
\q2 and all of our righteousnesses {are} like a menstrual rag.
\q1 And we have withered like a leaf, all of us,
\q2 and our iniquities carry us away like the wind.
\q1 \v 7 And there is none calling on your name,
\q2 awakening himself to hold onto you.
\q1 For you have hidden your face from us,
\q2 and you have melted us in the hand of our iniquities.
\b
\q1 \v 8 And now, Yahweh, you {are} our Father.
\q2 We {are} the clay, and you {are} our potter,
\q2 and all of us {are} the work of your hand.
\q1 \v 9 May you not be angry, Yahweh, to abundance,
\q2 and may you not remember iniquity forever.
\q2 Behold, please consider your people, all of us.
\q1 \v 10 The cities of your holiness have become a wilderness.
\q2 Zion has become a wilderness; Jerusalem, a devastation.
\q1 \v 11 The house of our holiness and our splendor,
\q2 where our fathers praised you,
\q2 has become a burning of fire,
\q2 and all of our precious things have become a desolation.
\q1 \v 12 At these, will you restrain yourself, Yahweh?
\q2 Will you be silent and humble us to abundance?”
\c 65
\q1 \v 1 “I was sought by they {who} did not ask;
\q2 I was found by they {who} did not seek me.
\q1 I said ‘Behold me! Behold me!’
\q2 to a nation, it was not called by my name.
\q1 \v 2 I spread out my hands all of the day
\q2 to a rebelling people,
\q1 ones walking {in} a way not good,
\q2 after their thoughts,
\q1 \v 3 a people provoking me to my face continually,
\q1 sacrificing in gardens
\q2 and burning incense on bricks,
\q1 \v 4 sitting among graves,
\q2 and they lodged in secret places,
\q1 eating the flesh of the pig,
\q2 and the broth of unclean things {was} in their vessels,
\q1 \v 5 saying, ‘Come near to yourself,
\q2 do not come near to me,
\q2 for I am holier than you.’
\q1 These {were} smoke in my nose,
\q2 a fire burning all of the day.
\q1 \v 6 Behold, it is written to my face,
\q2 I will not be silent, but I will repay,
\q2 and I will repay into their lap
\q1 \v 7 your iniquities and the iniquities of your fathers together,”
\q2 says Yahweh,
\q1 “because they have burned incense on the mountains
\q2 and have taunted me on the hills.
\q1 And I will measure their former deed
\q2 into their lap.”
\b
\q1 \v 8 Thus says Yahweh,
\q1 “As when juice is found in a cluster
\q2 and one says, ‘Do not destroy it,
\q2 for a blessing {is} in it,’
\q1 thus I will do for the sake of my servants,
\q2 so as not to destroy all.
\q1 \v 9 And I will bring out seed from Jacob,
\q2 and from Judah, a possessor of my mountains,
\q1 and my chosen ones will possess it,
\q2 and my servants will dwell there.
\q1 \v 10 And Sharon will be for a pasture of the flock,
\q2 and the Valley of Achor, for a lying down of the herd,
\q2 for my people who seek me.
\q1 \v 11 But you ones abandoning Yahweh,
\q2 forgetting the mountain of my holiness,
\q1 arranging a table for Fortune
\q2 and filling mixed wine for Destiny,
\q1 \v 12 indeed, I will appoint you for the sword,
\q2 and all of you will bow down to the slaughter,
\q1 because I called, but you did not answer;
\q2 I spoke, but you did not listen.
\q1 And you did evil in my eyes,
\q2 and in what I do not delight, you chose.”
\b
\q1 \v 13 Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh,
\q1 “Behold, my servants will eat,
\q2 but you, you will hunger.
\q1 Behold, my servants will drink,
\q2 but you, you will thirst.
\q1 Behold, my servants will rejoice,
\q2 but you, you will have shame.
\q1 \v 14 Behold, my servants will shout joyfully from goodness of heart,
\q2 but you, you will cry out from pain of heart,
\q2 and from breaking of spirit you will wail.
\q1 \v 15 And you will leave your name as a curse to my chosen ones,
\q2 and the Lord Yahweh will kill you,
\q2 but to his servants he will call another name.
\q1 \v 16 Whoever blesses himself in the land
\q2 will bless himself by the God of truth,
\q1 and the one swearing in the land
\q2 will swear by the God of truth,
\q1 for the former troubles will be forgotten,
\q2 for they will also be hidden from my eyes.
\q1 \v 17 For behold me, creating new heavens
\q2 and a new earth,
\q1 and the former {things} will not be remembered,
\q2 and they will not come up upon the heart.
\q1 \v 18 But rejoice and be glad until forever
\q2 {in} what I am creating,
\q1 for behold me, creating Jerusalem {as} a rejoicing
\q2 and its people {as} a joy.
\q1 \v 19 And I will be glad about Jerusalem,
\q2 and I will rejoice in my people,
\q1 and the sound of weeping and the sound of an outcry
\q2 will no longer be heard in it.
\b
\q1 \v 20 An infant of days will no longer be from there,
\q2 or an elder who does not fill his days,
\q1 for a young man will die {as} a son of 100 years,
\q2 and the one failing {to be} a son of 100 years will be cursed.
\q1 \v 21 And they will build houses, and they will dwell,
\q2 and they will plant vineyards, and they will eat their fruit.
\q1 \v 22 They will not build and another will dwell;
\q2 they will not plant and another will eat.
\q1 For the days of my people{will be} like the days of a tree,
\q2 and my chosen ones will wear out the work of their hands.
\q1 \v 23 They will not labor for worthlessness,
\q2 and they will not birth for terror,
\q1 for they {are} the seed of the blessed of Yahweh,
\q2 and their offspring with them.
\q1 \v 24 And it will happen, before they call, that I, I will answer;
\q2 they will still be speaking, and I, I will hear.
\q1 \v 25 The wolf and the lamb will graze as one,
\q2 and the lion will eat straw like the ox.
\q2 But the serpent, dust {will be} its bread.
\q1 They will not harm and they will not destroy
\q2 on all of the mountain of my holiness,”
\q2 says Yahweh.
\c 66
\p
\v 1 Thus says Yahweh,
\q1 “Heaven {is} my throne,
\q2 and the earth {is} the stool of my feet.
\q1 Where {is} this, the house that you will build for me?
\q2 And where {is} this, the place {of} my rest?
\q1 \v 2 For all of these, my hand has made;
\q2 so all of these are”
\q2 —the declaration of Yahweh.
\b
\q1 “And to this {one} I look,
\q2 to the humble and contrite of spirit,
\q2 and trembling at my word.
\q1 \v 3 The one slaughtering an ox is striking a man;
\q2 the one sacrificing a lamb is breaking the neck {of} a dog;
\q1 the one bringing up a grain offering, the blood of a pig;
\q2 the one making {one} remember incense is blessing nothingness.
\q1 As they, they have chosen their ways,
\q2 and their soul delights in their abominations,
\q1 \v 4 so I, I will choose their harsh treatments,
\q2 and I will bring their fears to them,
\q1 because I called, but none was answering;
\q2 I spoke, but they did not listen.
\q1 And they did evil in my eyes,
\q2 and they chose what I do not delight in.”
\b
\q1 \v 5 Hear the word of Yahweh,
\q2 ones trembling at his word:
\q1 “Your brothers, hating you,
\q2 excluding you for the sake of my name, have said,
\q1 ‘Let Yahweh be glorious,
\q2 that we may see your joy!’
\q2 But they, they will have shame.”`
\q1 \v 6 The sound of an uproar from the city!
\q2 A sound from the temple,
\q1 the sound of Yahweh
\q2 repaying recompense to his enemies!
\b
\q1 \v 7 Before she writhes, she births;
\q2 before pain comes to her, then she delivers a male.
\q1 \v 8 Who has heard like this?
\q2 Who has seen like these?
\q1 Will a land be writhed in one day?
\q2 Or will a nation be birthed {in} one moment?
\q1 For she writhed,
\q2 Zion also birthed her sons.
\q1 \v 9 “I, will I break open and not cause to birth?” says Yahweh.
\q2 “Or I am causing birth, then will I restrain?” says your God.
\q1 \v 10 Rejoice with Jerusalem
\q2 and be glad with her, all lovers of her!
\q1 Rejoice with her {in} gladness,
\q2 all ones mourning over her,
\q1 \v 11 so that you may nurse and have satisfaction
\q2 from the breast of her consolations,
\q1 so that you may suck and be refreshed
\q2 from the abundance of her glory.
\p
\v 12 For thus says Yahweh:
\q1 “Behold me, extending peace to her like a river,
\q2 and like an overflowing stream, the glory of the nations,
\q1 and you will nurse.
\q2 You will be carried on {her} side,
\q2 and you will be bounced on{her} knees.
\q1 \v 13 Like a man whose mother comforts him,
\q2 so I, I will comfort you,
\q2 and you will be comforted in Jerusalem.”
\b
\q1 \v 14 And you will see, and your heart will rejoice,
\q2 and your bones will blossom like the grass,
\q1 and the hand of Yahweh will be made known to his servants,
\q2 but he will be indignant against his enemies.
\q1 \v 15 For behold, Yahweh will come with fire,
\q2 and his chariots, like a windstorm,
\q1 to render his nose with heat,
\q2 and his rebuke, in flames of fire.
\q1 \v 16 For Yahweh is judging with fire
\q2 and by his sword against all flesh,
\q2 and the slain of Yahweh will be many.
\p
\v 17 “The ones consecrating themselves and the ones purifying themselves to the gardens after the one in the midst, eaters of the flesh of the pig and the abomination and the mouse, they will end together”—the declaration of Yahweh.
\p
\v 18 “And I—their deeds and their thoughts—it is coming, to gather all of the nations and languages, and they will come and see my glory.
\v 19 And I will set a sign among them, and I will send fugitives from them to the nations—Tarshish, Pul, and Lud, drawers of the bow, Tubal and Javan, the distant coastlands—that have not heard my report and have not seen my glory, and they will declare my glory among the nations.
\v 20 And they will bring all of your brothers from all of the nations {as} an offering to Yahweh, on horses and in chariots and in wagons and on mules and on camels, to the mountain of my holiness, Jerusalem,” says Yahweh, “just as the sons of Israel bring the grain offering in a clean vessel {to} the house of Yahweh.
\v 21 And I will also take from them as priests, as Levites,” says Yahweh.
\b
\q1 \v 22 “For just as the new heavens and the new earth
\q2 that I am making are standing to my face”—the declaration of Yahweh—
\q1 “thus your seed and your name will stand.
\q1 \v 23 And it will be, from new moon to its new moon
\q2 and from Sabbath to its Sabbath,
\q1 all flesh will come to bow down
\q2 to my face,” says Yahweh.
\q1 \v 24 “And they will go out and see
\q2 the corpses of the men having rebelled against me,
\q1 for their worm will not die
\q2 and their fire will not go out,
\q2 and they will be an abhorrence to all flesh.” 